  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 759075,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 10 Years Arse: A Chronicle of Repression (Commodore 64)\n\nTen years have passed since Winston Smith’s rebellion. Oceania remains under the iron grip of the Party, but the embers of dissent still flicker. *10 Years Arse* plunges you into this grim reality as a nameless citizen, haunted by fragmented memories of the past and driven by a desperate yearning for freedom.\n\nThis challenging platformer, inspired by Orwell’s *1984*, sees you navigating the decaying urban landscape of London, evading the ever-watchful eyes of the Thought Police and their robotic enforcers.  Gameplay focuses on precise jumps, stealth, and resource management – food and medicine are scarce, and every encounter carries the risk of capture and re-education.\n\nUncover hidden messages and snippets of forbidden knowledge left behind by previous rebels, piecing together the truth about the Party’s continued control.  The game features a haunting soundtrack and minimalist graphics, perfectly capturing the oppressive atmosphere of Oceania.  Can you survive the surveillance, resist the indoctrination, and perhaps, just perhaps, spark a new flame of hope?"
    },
